fix(auth): resolve google login blank screen, registration error, and logout redirect

# --- Problem Solved / Strategic Objective ---
- Google login with existing account (kevingkday@gmail.com) led to a blank white screen because user array fields (servicesOffered, targetIndustries, targetRoles) stored as JSON strings in SQLite were not parsed into arrays by sanitizeUser, causing ProfilePage and OnboardingModal to throw TypeError when calling .map() or .join().
- Google registration with a new account (kevin@oceanfallsinsurance.com) failed with a "Network connection error" because the D1 production database was missing migration 0011_buyer_profile.sql (causing SQLite "no such column: service_area" 500 error, which resulted in unhandled non-JSON responses in AuthModal).
- Signing out left the user on the previous view rather than navigating back to the home landing page and resetting the URL hash/query.

# --- Implementation Details ---
- server/drizzle/migrations:
  - Synchronized d1_migrations table on remote D1 and applied 0011_buyer_profile.sql to provision buyer profile columns.
- server/src/routes/auth.ts:
  - Added parseJsonArray to sanitizeUser so user profile fields (servicesOffered, productsOffered, targetIndustries, targetRoles, buyerIndustries, buyerRoles) are returned as proper arrays to the client.
- client/src/components/ErrorBoundary.tsx:
  - Added application Error Boundary with friendly recovery UI to prevent future unhandled React crashes from rendering blank screens.
- client/src/App.tsx:
  - Wrapped root views with ErrorBoundary.
  - Updated handleLogout to redirect currentView to 'landing' and clear hash and query parameters.
- client/src/components/ProfilePage.tsx & OnboardingModal.tsx:
  - Added ensureArray guards on array state variables to prevent runtime crashes when parsing tags.
- client/src/components/ExecutiveAvatar.tsx & utils/buyerProfile.ts:
  - Added null/undefined guards on name string length and input.targetIndustries.
- client/src/components/AuthModal.tsx:
  - Improved Google auth error handling to surface exact server error text instead of throwing a generic network error.

# --- Verification & Testing ---
- [x] Type check verified: npm run typecheck passed (client Vite build + server tsc).
- [x] Security and unit tests verified: npm test --prefix server passed all 25 tests.
- [x] Remote database verified: 0011_buyer_profile.sql applied and confirmed via PRAGMA table_info.
- [x] Cloudflare Workers deployment: successfully built and deployed via npm run deploy to https://twinflow.kevin-c8e.workers.dev.
